  5. [38;5;153mdueDate[39m within today..today+2 → [1m[38;5;153mdue-soon[0m

  Sorted overdue-first, oldest first. The due-soon window is a module constant, not a preference — no settings UI until
  you want one.

  Dates compare [1mdate-only in local time[0m, derived from the injected [38;5;153mnow[39m. Comparing a date-only string against a UTC
  timestamp is the classic off-by-one in this feature; keeping both sides date-only in one timezone avoids it outright.

  [1m4. Delivery surface[0m

  A panel rendered above the task list inside [38;5;153m<main>[39m:

  - Summary line: [3m"2 overdue · 1 due soon"[0m
  - One row per notification: task title, how late/soon, and a [1mSnooze 1 day[0m button
  - Renders nothing at all when the list is empty — no empty-state chrome
  - Recomputed on every state change [1mand[0m on a 60-second timer, so a task crossing its deadline surfaces without a reload

  [1mExplicitly out of scope:[0m the browser Notification API / OS toasts. It costs a permission prompt, only works while the
  tab is open, and adds nothing over a panel you're already looking at. Easy to add later if you want it.

